      <title>How Kansans are supporting each other through Parkinson's disease</title>
      <link>https://www.kcur.org/podcast/kansas-city-today/2026-02-04/how-kansans-are-supporting-each-other-through-parkinsons-disease</link>
      <description>Kansas has one of the highest rates of Parkinson’s disease diagnoses. Groups there are helping people slow the progression of the disease through activities including exercise and art classes. Plus: Nipple tattoos are an option for the many American women who survive breast cancer and end their treatment looking for a way to reconnect with themselves and their bodies.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.kcur.org/podcast/kansas-city-today/2026-02-04/how-kansans-are-supporting-each-other-through-parkinsons-disease</guid>
